IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc7-order-33b`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore): TESTS for roc7-order-33b.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the rule named after each assertion (the comment on its line),
-- never copied from what the code printed.  The gate-shaped rules (a MAYBE BOOLEAN over BOOLEAN conditions) are tested
-- by the kind of the rule: every condition met; then each condition missing in turn.


-- Hand-written tests for Order 33 rules 18 to 28.  Generated assertions (gates and periods) follow.

-- r 18(1)
#ASSERT `o 33 r 18(1) the provisions of this Rule apply to the action` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a collision claim, no contrary order
#ASSERT `o 33 r 18(1) the provisions of this Rule apply to the action` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "unless the Court otherwise orders"
#ASSERT `o 33 r 18(1) the provisions of this Rule apply to the action` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- another kind of action: not answered

-- r 18(2): the preliminary act, every paragraph both ways
#ASSERT `o 33 r 18(2) Part One states every matter in paragraphs (a) to (q)` (`o 33 r 18(2) preliminary act` WITH `o 33 r 18(2)(a) states the names of the ships and their ports of registry` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(b) states the dimensions of the ship and its cargo` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(c) states the date and time of the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(d) states the place of the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(e) states the wind` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(f) states the weather` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(g) states the tidal or other current` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(h) states the position, course and speed when the other ship was first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(i) states the lights or shapes carried` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(j) states the radar echo of the other ship` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(k) states the other ship when first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(l) states the light or shape of the other ship first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(m) states the other lights or shapes subsequently seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(n) states the alterations and measures taken to avoid the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(o) states the heading, the points of contact and the angle` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(p) states the sound signals given` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(q) states the sound signals heard` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(r) states that the particulars in Part One are incorporated in Part Two` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(s) states any other facts relied on` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(t) states the allegations of negligence or other fault` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(u) states the remedy or relief claimed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all of (a) to (q) stated
#ASSERT `o 33 r 18(2) Part Two states every matter in paragraphs (r) to (u)` (`o 33 r 18(2) preliminary act` WITH `o 33 r 18(2)(a) states the names of the ships and their ports of registry` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(b) states the dimensions of the ship and its cargo` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(c) states the date and time of the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(d) states the place of the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(e) states the wind` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(f) states the weather` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(g) states the tidal or other current` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(h) states the position, course and speed when the other ship was first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(i) states the lights or shapes carried` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(j) states the radar echo of the other ship` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(k) states the other ship when first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(l) states the light or shape of the other ship first seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(m) states the other lights or shapes subsequently seen` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(n) states the alterations and measures taken to avoid the collision` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(o) states the heading, the points of contact and the angle` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(p) states the sound signals given` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(q) states the sound signals heard` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(r) states that the particulars in Part One are incorporated in Part Two` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(s) states any other facts relied on` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(t) states the allegations of negligence or other fault` IS TRUE, `o 33 r 18(2)(u) states the remedy or relief claimed` IS TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all of (r) to (u) stated
